Cloudflare Worker REST API for Turso/libSQL (React-Admin Simple REST
compatible). ## Deploy ```bash pnpm install pnpm exec wrangler secret put
API_KEY pnpm exec wrangler secret put TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN pnpm run deploy ``` For
local dev, `wrangler dev` reads `API_KEY` and `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` from
`.dev.vars`, and `TURSO_CONNECTION_URL` from the `vars` block in
`wrangler.jsonc`. ## Resource configuration The resource config in
`src/index.ts` defines which database columns are exposed via the API
(`selectableFields`, `filterableFields`, `sortableFields`, `searchableFields`).
If you did not use `--auto-discover`, only the `id` column is configured per
table. Edit `src/index.ts` to add the remaining columns, or re-run the CLI with
`--auto-discover` to introspect your schema automatically. ## Configure
React-Admin ```ts import { createTursoDataProvider } from "ra-turso"; const
dataProvider = createTursoDataProvider({ apiUrl: "https://YOUR_WORKER_URL/api",
// This runs in the browser: provide the API key via your bundler env (e.g. //
import.meta.env.VITE_API_KEY). apiKey: import.meta.env.VITE_API_KEY, }); ``` >
**Security note:** The API key is sent from the browser and is therefore >
public. It deters casual traffic but is not a true secret. For production, >
consider putting the Worker behind Cloudflare Access or another auth layer.